    "chunk_text": "Sri Lanka Broadcasting Corporation Technical Officers\u2019 Union, Sri Lanka Broadcasting Corporation,Colombo 07.of the one part\n\nand\n\nSri Lanka Broadcasting Corporation, Independent Square, Colombo 07.of the other part\n\nRAVINDRA SAMARAWEERA,Minister of Labour and Trade Union Relations.\n\nColombo,19th September, 2019.\n\nI fldgi: (I) fPoh \u2013 Y%S ,xld m%cd;dka;%sl iudcjd\u00a7 ckrcfha w;s \u00fafYI .ei\u00dc m;%h \u2013 2019'09'27PART I: SEC. (I) \u2013 GAZETTE EXTRAORDINARY OF THE DEMOCRATIC SOCIALIST REPUBLIC OF SRI LANKA \u2013 27.09.20193A\n\nPRINTED AT THE DEPARTMENT OF GOVERNMENT PRINTING, SRI LANKA\n\nMy No.: IR/COM/05/2018/270.\n\nTHE INDUSTRIAL DISPUTES ACT, CHAPTER 131 OF THE LEGISLATIVE EN ACTMENTS OF CEYLON(1956 REVISED EDITION)\n\nSri Lanka Broadcasting Corporation Technical Officers\u2019 Union, Sri Lanka Broadcasting Corporation,Colombo 07.of the one part\n\nand\n\nSri Lanka Broadcasting Corporation, Independent Square, Colombo 07.of the other part\n\nSTATEMENT OF MATTER IN DISPUTE\n\nThe matter in dispute between the aforesaid parties is\n\nWhether the Technical Assistants (including the Officers in Charge) of Grade I in a Salary Code similar to JM-1-1 have beencaused injustice by not being placed in MM-1-1 salary code in the Salary Revision of year 2018 for the approved cadre of theSri Lanka Broadcasting Corporation even though some posts in the JM-1-1 salary code have been placed in the MM-1-1 salarycode and if such injustice had been caused, to what relief they are entitled.\n\nA. WIMALAWEERA,Commissioner General of Labour.\n\nDated at the office of the Commissioner General of Labour,Colombo, this 26th day of August, 2019.\n\n10 \u2013 488"
