    "chunk_text": "WHEN the Election Commission decides that it is necessary to inquire further into the information or complaints receivedby it regarding the violation of an order or orders issued by the Election Commission to prevent the misuse of governmentproperty in connection with the election and orders to submit relevant print or electronic documents, discussion notes,reports including those relating to the recruitment or appointment, to the Election Commission or of an officer authorizedby the Election Commission, public officers in charge of such documents should take action to provide all relevantinformation. In such instances when the Election Commission or an officer authorized by the Election Commissionorders to submit any oral or written statement for further inquiries into an incident where any order or orders issued bythe Election Commission have been violated, relevant public officers should be responsible for providing all-inclusivestatements. They are bound to do so.\n\nIn all the places where the government is referred to in these orders, it refers to all government institutionsincluding ministries, departments, provincial councils, local authorities, state corporations, statutory boards, commissions,state banks, state universities, state-owned companies and institutions morethan 50% of whose shares, are owned bygovernment or state-owned corporations.\n\nI fldgi ( ^I& fPoh - YS% ,xld m%cd;dka;s%l iudcjd\u00a7 ckrcfha w;s \u00fafYI .ei\u00dc m;%h - 2019'10'03PART I : SEC. (I) - GAZETTE EXTRAORDINARY OF THE DEMOCRATIC SOCIALIST REPUBLIC OF SRI LANKA - 03.10.20192A\n\n\u201cPublic Officers and Employees\u201d in all places means all persons engaged or employed at the said institutionsand are receiving a remuneration or allowance.\n\nInterpretation of \u201cInformation\u201d in the Right to Information Act No. 12 of 2016 applies to the \u201cInformation\u201dreferred to in these orders.\n\nThe Gazette Extraordinary No. 2048/2 dated 04.12.2017 issued in this regard is hereby rescinded."
